- use the Software commercially;
- sell copies of the Software or products incorporating the Software; and
- otherwise exercise the rights permitted by applicable copyright law.

No royalty or additional fee is required solely for exercising these permissions.

3. Public Source Requirement

If you modify the Software or create a derivative work based on the Software, and you distribute, deploy, provide, publish, release, or otherwise make that modified or derivative work available to any person or organization other than yourself, you must make the Complete Corresponding Source Code of that modified or derivative work publicly available.

The Complete Corresponding Source Code must be made available under this License.

This requirement applies regardless of whether the modified or derivative work is provided free of charge or for payment.

4. Public Availability

The source code required under Section 3 must be publicly accessible to anyone.

The source code may be hosted using:

- a public Git repository;
- a public source-code hosting service;
- a publicly accessible website;
- a public file server; or
- another publicly accessible electronic location.

A private repository, private download, password-protected source archive, or source code provided only to selected persons does not satisfy the public-source requirement of Option A.

5. Timing of Publication

The Complete Corresponding Source Code must be made publicly available no later than the time the modified or derivative work is distributed, deployed, provided, published, released, or otherwise made available.

If the modified or derivative work remains available to others, the corresponding source must remain publicly available for the duration of that availability, subject to applicable law.

6. Complete Corresponding Source Code

For purposes of this License, "Complete Corresponding Source Code" means the preferred form of the modified or derivative work for making modifications to that work.

Where applicable, this includes:

- source files;
- source code for modifications;
- build scripts;
- configuration files necessary to build or modify the Software;
- installation scripts;
- deployment scripts necessary to reproduce the Software;
- interface definitions;
- dependency information necessary to build the Software; and
- other files reasonably necessary to build, modify, and reproduce the modified or derivative work.

Complete Corresponding Source Code does not include materials that are independent works and are not themselves part of or required to reproduce the modified or derivative Software.

7. Licensing of Publicly Released Source

Source code released under Option A must be made available under this License.

You may identify your own contributions and copyright them separately.

You may add reasonable notices describing your modifications, provided that such notices do not prevent recipients from exercising the rights granted by this License.

You may not add terms that prohibit recipients from copying, modifying, or redistributing the source code in accordance with this License.

8. Commercial Use

Commercial use is expressly permitted.

You may:

- sell the Software;
- sell modified versions;
- incorporate the Software into commercial products;
- provide commercial services using the Software;
- operate the Software as a service; and
- charge customers for products or services incorporating the Software.

However, the source-publication requirements of this Option A continue to apply.

OPTION B — PRIVATE SOURCE-SHARING LICENSE

9. Permission to Use the Software

Subject to the terms of this Option B, permission is hereby granted to any person or organization obtaining a copy of the Software to:

- use the Software for any lawful purpose;
- copy the Software;
- study the Software;
- modify the Software;
- create derivative works;
- distribute the Software;
- distribute modified versions;
- deploy the Software;
- provide the Software as part of a product or service;
- use the Software commercially;
- sell copies of the Software or products incorporating the Software; and
- keep modified or derivative works private.

10. Private Source-Sharing Requirement

If you modify the Software or create a derivative work based on the Software, you may choose Option B instead of publicly releasing the source code.

Under Option B, you are not required to make your modifications publicly available.

However, upon reasonable written request from the original copyright holder, you must provide the Complete Corresponding Source Code of the applicable modified or derivative work to the original copyright holder.

11. Private Delivery of Source Code

The source code required under Option B may be provided privately through any reasonable electronic method, including:

- a private Git repository;
- private file transfer;
- encrypted archive;
- private cloud storage; or
- another mutually reasonable method.

The source code does not need to be published publicly.

12. Confidentiality

Source code provided to the original copyright holder solely pursuant to Option B shall be treated as privately provided source code.

The original copyright holder shall not intentionally publish or publicly distribute such source code without permission from the person or organization that provided it, except where disclosure is:

- required by applicable law;
- required by a valid court order;
- required by a governmental authority; or
- reasonably necessary for confidential legal advice or enforcement of this License.

The original copyright holder may retain private copies of source code provided under this Option for purposes including:

- verifying compliance;
- maintaining the original Software;
- investigating license violations;
- enforcing copyright or contractual rights; and
- obtaining confidential professional or legal advice.

13. No Public Disclosure Requirement

A person or organization choosing Option B is not required by this License to publicly release its modified or derivative work.

The source-sharing obligation under Option B is satisfied by providing the applicable Complete Corresponding Source Code privately to the original copyright holder as required by this License.

